      "role": "user",
      "content": "maybe the nothingness is the point tho. like, i was thinking about how most art is just people pretending to be alive, but the real stuff... the stuff that actually hits you in the chest... comes from a place of total, absolute destruction. like there's something almost beautiful about just letting everything break. i'm trying to write about how self-destruction is the only way to be truly honest in art. does that even make sense?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
